WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.051
Insurance Pricing estimates annual
charges and explains every estimate.

2
00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:08.323
Good pricing models are often a black box.

3
00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.974
They are hard for non-technical
stakeholders to interpret.

4
00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:14.577
It estimates annual charges.

5
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.436
It explains how each
detail moved the estimate.

6
00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.175
And it interprets the result
in plain language.

7
00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:25.881
Here is one sample applicant:
48, a smoker, with two children.

8
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.206
Six details go in,
and one estimate comes out.

9
00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:35.927
A trained model puts her
estimate at about $33,000 a year.

10
00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:41.887
Each bar shows how one detail
moved the estimate, up or down.

11
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:44.771
Smoking adds the most.

12
00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:49.295
A language model then writes
the reasons in plain English.

13
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:51.060
Here, they match the chart.

14
00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.216
Now change one detail.

15
00:00:54.216 --> 00:00:55.438
She does not smoke.

16
00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:57.937
Estimate again.

17
00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:02.637
The estimate falls by about $23,000.

18
00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:09.192
Not smoking now pulls
the estimate down the most.

19
00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:13.314
The estimate, the bars
and the reasons all update.

20
00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:15.667
Insurance Pricing.

21
00:01:15.667 --> 00:01:18.645
Every estimate comes
with the reasons behind it.
